---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Elsewhere" active="Elsewhere" description="Beyond physics: creative projects, community, travel, and interests">

  <section class="page-header page-header-video">
    <div class="video-bg">
      <iframe
        src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/g6quT1AjrTg?autoplay=1&mute=1&loop=1&playlist=g6quT1AjrTg&controls=0&rel=0&modestbranding=1"
        allow="autoplay; encrypted-media"
        title="Sacred Architectures documentary"
      ></iframe>
    </div>
    <div class="video-overlay"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Elsewhere</h1>
      <p>On things beyond physics</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── CREATIVE PROJECTS ─────────────────── -->
  <section class="elsewhere-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Creative Projects</span>

      <div class="elsewhere-project">
        <div class="elsewhere-project-header">
          <h2>Mycopoetica</h2>
          <span class="elsewhere-year">2022</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          A poetry collection exploring fungi's role in climate change through the lens of absurdist
          philosophy and thematic verse. Ten poems structured to provoke critical reflection on ecological
          collapse, decomposition, and regeneration, with planned multimedia extensions. Written for
          <em>Performing Science: Experimentation, Collaboration, and Artistry</em>, my freshman fall course at Duke.
        </p>
        <div class="elsewhere-links">
          <a href="/projects/MycoPoetica - Karna, Abhishek - 2022.pdf" target="_blank" class="btn">
            <i class="fas fa-file-pdf"></i> Read Collection
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="elsewhere-project">
        <div class="elsewhere-project-header">
          <h2>Sacred Architectures</h2>
          <span class="elsewhere-year">2023–24</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Field research documenting over 100 temples across South India and more than 15 in Cambodia,
          tracing the architectural and religious exchange between Dravidian and Khmer traditions. The
          project produced a multimedia poster, <em>South Asia's Sacred Temples: A Dive into the
          Ethno-Geographical and Transcultural Religious Exchange</em>, and a documentary-style trailer
          on the Dravidian–Khmer architectural dialogue.
        </p>
        <div class="elsewhere-links">
          <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=g6quT1AjrTg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-primary">
            <i class="fab fa-youtube"></i> Documentary Trailer
          </a>
          <a href="/projects/Dravidian-Khmer Field Project - Karna, Abhishek - 2023_24.pdf" target="_blank" class="btn">
            <i class="fas fa-file-pdf"></i> Research Poster
          </a>
          <a href="/projects/Conferences - OUSF Poster Session - Karna, Abhishek.pdf" target="_blank" class="btn">
            <i class="fas fa-file-pdf"></i> OUSF Session
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── COMMUNITY ─────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="elsewhere-section alt">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Community</span>

      <div class="elsewhere-project">
        <div class="elsewhere-project-header">
          <h2>Duke Nepali Students Association</h2>
          <span class="elsewhere-year">2022–26</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Founding President. Brought together 40+ Nepali-origin students and staff at Duke, organized
          10+ cultural and community events, networked with the Nepali diaspora across North Carolina,
          and engaged the broader Duke community with Nepali culture.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="elsewhere-project">
        <div class="elsewhere-project-header">
          <h2>Duke in Geneva</h2>
          <span class="elsewhere-year">2024</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Studied International Business and the Political Philosophy of Globalization as part of Duke's
          Study Away Program. Visited the UN, Palais des Nations, UNHCR, ILO, WHO, WTO, and CERN.
          Traveled across Switzerland, France, Italy, and several other European countries for field
          experiences in Philosophy, Politics, and Economics.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── INTERESTS ─────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="elsewhere-section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Interests</span>

      <div class="interests-grid">

        <div class="interest-item">
          <div class="interest-icon"><i class="fas fa-book-open"></i></div>
          <div>
            <h3>Philosophy</h3>
            <p>Particularly Non-Dualism and the philosophy of mind. The essays I write will draw heavily on this.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="interest-item">
          <div class="interest-icon"><i class="fas fa-music"></i></div>
          <div>
            <h3>Music</h3>
            <p>Singing and acoustic guitar. Mostly folk, classical Nepali, and whatever I'm currently obsessed with.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="interest-item">
          <div class="interest-icon"><i class="fas fa-mountain"></i></div>
          <div>
            <h3>Outdoors</h3>
            <p>Trekking and hiking. I grew up near the Himalayas, so the bar is high.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="interest-item">
          <div class="interest-icon"><i class="fas fa-cricket-ball" style="font-size:0.9rem;"></i></div>
          <div>
            <h3>Cricket</h3>
            <p>Duke Intramural Leagues Cricket Championship, 2025.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="interest-item">
          <div class="interest-icon"><i class="fas fa-plane"></i></div>
          <div>
            <h3>Travel</h3>
            <p>South Asia, Southeast Asia, Europe. Usually in pursuit of temples, food, or conferences. Ideally all three.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="interest-item">
          <div class="interest-icon"><i class="fas fa-seedling"></i></div>
          <div>
            <h3>Mycology</h3>
            <p>Started with Mycopoetica, hasn't stopped. Fungi are genuinely the most interesting organisms on Earth.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
